# The ONE place tool names live.  Format:  name  [timeout_seconds]  [net]
#   timeout_seconds: default 30, max 120
#   net: the literal word net gives that tool the sandbox's network namespace
#        (bwrap --share-net). Without it the tool runs with no network. What a
#        network tool can reach is still decided by the core's firewall. The
#        console writes a timeout explicitly; `name net` is also accepted.
#
# Disable a tool by commenting it out:  # off: name [timeout_seconds] [net]
#
# Add a tool:
#   1. add a line here, e.g. `fetch 30 net` for a tool that needs the network
#   2. write sbx/tools/<name>/run              (runs on the sandbox box)
#   3. write harness/tools/<name>-sbx/tcs.yaml (the contract, on the trusted box)
#   4. python3 sync.py                         (generates the stub, validates everything)
#   5. deploy: this file -> /etc/sbx/tools.list (harness) and /opt/sbx/tools.list (sbx)
greet   10
rsync   120 net
